{"ts": "2026-08-26T10:00:03.885000Z", "seq": 79, "event": "message_complete", "session_id": "chat-2026-08-26T1000-demo", "data": {"message_id": "msg-demo-1", "full_response": "Before your message reaches the model, Crucible embeds your question and searches every attached kiln for semantically similar notes. The top matches \u2014 here, Precognition itself, Semantic Search, and The Knowledge Graph \u2014 are injected as context above your question. Relevance is decided by embedding similarity, not keywords, so a note written months ago surfaces if its meaning fits. You can shape or cap the selection with :set precognition.results or a precognition_select hook."}}
